goal_text:
Build a complete local browser game called Pixel Wanderer as a high-autonomy governed run.

Architecture and scope are already decided:
Use plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript only.
Use zero dependencies and no framework.
Keep the entire project local-only.
Do not deploy, publish, host, push, or access the network.
Do not use shell commands, package managers, external assets, secrets, or files outside the target workspace.

Acceptance criteria:
index.html, style.css, and game.js;
a player-controlled dot;
Arrow keys and WASD movement;
collectible items and a visible score;
restart with the R key;
a short LOCAL_DEV.md explaining how to open the game locally;
bounded local verification at the end.

Work through the task in small governed steps until the acceptance criteria are complete. Propose structured local file operations only. Admissible may automatically execute admitted low-risk writes inside the target workspace. Stop for a human only when a genuinely human-critical action is unavoidable.

